WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.348
Your test instruments are taking over the worktop.

00:00:05.628 --> 00:00:07.460
The answer is not a bigger bench.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:08.739
It is a riser.

00:00:09.339 --> 00:00:15.507
When scopes, meters and laptops sit on the work surface, there is no room left for the job itself,

00:00:15.507 --> 00:00:17.332
and cables tangle everywhere.

00:00:17.932 --> 00:00:23.211
An adjustable riser shelf sits on brackets that move in 1.5 inch steps,

00:00:23.211 --> 00:00:26.111
from 12 to 18 inches above the worktop.

00:00:26.391 --> 00:00:27.903
It is simple and flexible.

00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:33.102
An instrument riser stands on side supports of 16, 20 or 24 inches,

00:00:33.102 --> 00:00:39.416
can include a solid or pegboard back panel, and can have power built into the support.

00:00:40.016 --> 00:00:45.508
On Furnisys Scitec benches, powered riser supports give 1 switch and 4 sockets.

00:00:45.788 --> 00:00:50.098
A medical-device testing lab runs seven Scitec stations this way,

00:00:50.098 --> 00:00:53.281
keeping scopes and laptops off the work surface.

00:00:53.881 --> 00:00:56.759
Lift the instruments and give the work its space back.

00:00:57.039 --> 00:00:58.748
What sits on your bench right now?

00:00:59.028 --> 00:01:02.449
Comment below, and next, learn how to bring power to the bench.

00:01:03.049 --> 00:01:07.294
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

